hi and welcome back to rapid fire  language learning  today we're going to explore the  question how to think directly in your  target language  when we speak a foreign language we want  to sound sophisticated as if  we were speaking our own native language  but sometimes we don't have the tools if  we don't speak that language still  fluently so my piece of advice is to  simplify  to the bone if you have to say something  like for example i want to go to japan  because i've never been to japan before  make sure that you just break down the  sentence into two smaller sentences  because  the smaller the sentence the more  manageable it is something along the  lines of for example  i want to go to japan i've never been  there then you can use conjunctions  to progressively connect these simple  pieces  of content and form longer sentences  remember simple does not mean simplistic  if you apply this especially to  languages that have a different syntax  and a different  sentence structure then things warm up  pretty quickly  thanks for watching over and out
 

